{"event":"pre-tool-use","timestamp":"2026-10-20T18:45:40.242Z","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd 'D:/Dev/senior-full-stack-with-unity-ai-code-challenge/.claude/worktrees/stratus-field-link-exercise-07ba02' && (cd src/StratusFieldLink.Api.Tests && dotnet test 2>&1 | grep -E \"Passed!|Failed!\") && U=unity/StratusFieldLink/Assets/StratusFieldLink && git add $U/Runtime/Model/SketchDtos.cs $U/Runtime/Net/PublishQueue.cs $U/Runtime/Net/PublishService.cs $U/Tests/EditMode/PublishQueueTests.cs $U/Tests/PlayMode/PublishFlowTests.cs && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfeat(unity): survive a bad network with a persisted, draining publish queue\n\nPublishService now decides per answer: 2xx removes the sketch from the queue\n(200 = duplicate, still a success); no signal queues and persists it\n(QueuedOffline); 5xx queues it for up to 3 retries (QueuedForRetry) and then\nholds it; any 4xx is reported with the server's reason and, for a queued\nsketch, held. A held sketch (409, other 4xx, retries exhausted) stays on the\ndevice but is never auto-resent. DrainQueue runs at start-up and after any\nsuccessful publish, stops at the first network failure, and republishing a\nsketch under the same id replaces the held copy.\n\nFieldSketchDto gains retryCount and holdReason (client-side bookkeeping).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -4","timeout":240000,"description":"Run API suite and commit Task 2"}}
